The gentleman/lady (adventurer) is taking shape. Right now you get one
of two flavors, one equipped with a machete, pith helmet, tall boots,
and a backpack ... the other equipped with a walking stick, deerhunter
hat (the "Sherlock Holmes" hat), tweed jacket, sack, and so on.

I feel the need for a Lost World / Center of the Earth branch. With
dinosaurs, cavemen, cavewomen (in bikinis presumably), Dr. Livingston,
giant man-eating plants, sea monsters, and perhaps some dude gone
native as the chief (or just a chief). I hacked in an outdoor-style
test level with trees and water and all, and accidentally left it
dark. It's entertaining walking around "outside" in the dark with no
lamp when pools and lakes are scattered about. I think I need to add a
beach/sand tile, if I can find an appropriate character for it. Also I
need to write an appropriate map generator.

Maybe there could be water levels with a boat/raft you could get
into?  Apply canoe toward water ... "you get into the canoe",
"something bumps the underside of your canoe," "the giant squid wraps
its tentacles around your canoe!", "your canoe is being pulled under,"
"you hit the giant squid! It lets go of your canoe," etc.

Also, insect repellent. "The huge mosquito hits! It draws blood! You
feel weaker."



